      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MAYSOONFLY (4) has been consistently close without winning, beaten just over a length at her past two starts at this venue, and the held-up second to Kayla Kruzen reads well for this. Ready to win. KISS AND KABOOM (7) can threaten despite a plain first-up tenth in a BM58 at Balaklava, with her record at this track and distance the key reason to give her another chance. She has one win and two placings from four attempts over this course and trip, draws barrier 1 and drops into a more suitable Class 1 assignment. Key runner. SUPER CHOICE (1) brings solid BM56 form, was fourth at Murray Bridge last start and is proven around 1200m, though the quick back-up and rise from 1000m keep him more in the place mix. SIR CASTLETON (3) resumes from six months off, has had two trials since last racing and won his only start at this track, so he has enough profile to run well fresh if ready. Include.",
